  "details": "This is a post dedicated for discussion about various VRChat connection issues in Russia.\n\n# **The Problems:**\n\nRight now, most connection issues can be split into three categories:\n\n1. VRChat services isn't accessible at all or partially due to large CDNs bans (Cloudflare) by RKN. Symptoms:\n\n- VRChat web site isn't loading or loading partially.\n\n- Can't login into VRChat on its start (just empty green screen, no errors);\n\n- Some API responses isn't loading (Friends, world lists, ...);\n\n- Assets (including images on the site) isn't loading\n\n2. VRChat blocks some VPNs, so services aren't accessible. Symptoms:\n\n- Can't login into VRChat on its start (just empty green screen, no errors);\n\n- VRChat shows errors about IP being blocked.\n\n3. General connection interruptions. Symptoms:\n\n- Can login and connect instances but randomly disconnects from the instance once per few minutes.\n\n# **Workarounds:**\n\n- Using own x-ray / amneziawg VPN on own \"high-quality\" VPS. (Tutorial in Russian: https://notes.vard.cc/tutorials/making_vpn_server )\n\n- \"undpi\" Cloudflare WARP using Zapret (Tutorial in Russian: https://steamcommunity.com/app/438100/discussions/0/600780778224284219/ ); Confirmed: not working everywhere in Russia, only in some regions and ISPs.\n\n- Using Cloudflare WARP over VPN or VPS (to be written)\n\n# **Where to get help:**\n\n- VRChatRU Discord: https://discord.com/invite/Kw55MAU (Threads about issues: https://discord.com/channels/666306330230915093/1381922723004944394 , https://discord.com/channels/666306330230915093/1382230220668534867 , thread about VPNs: https://discord.com/channels/666306330230915093/1306550460777234452 )\n\n- VRChatRU Telegram: https://t.me/vrcru\n\n(Пожалуйста, не спамьте в главный чат, есть чаты для помощи)\n\n# **Gathering information: **\n\nPlease, **drop info on your problems and solutions** in the comments.\n\nПожалуйста, **опубликуйте информацию о ваших проблемах и их решениях** в комментариях.\n\n= = =\n\n# **To VRChat Team: **\n\n= = =\n\nAs you can see in the comments, **there is entire zoo of various errors**, most of them **non informative** at all and/or **breaks VRChat until full restart**.\n\nIn most cases, when connection with the instance isn't interrupted, I see **no reason to not simply re-connect** to the API and websockets in background just making passive non modal info popup about connection being re-established.\n\n**VRChat should not hang or lock itself due bad connectivity and must be sustainable.**",
